   "id": "SI-1",
   "severity": "resolved-by-root-correction (integration defect caused by my v2 class change)",
   "title": "Name-based SEAL adapter catch let the typed replay-mismatch condition escape as a host exception",
   "evidence": "root-final38-reference.v1 evaluator3 child analysis-seal exited 1: identity close_run raised security_identity_model_v3.CompleteReplayMismatch for the reminted semantically false Run, and the adapter matched only the names AdmissionError/EvidenceUnavailable/RegenerationMismatch. Reproduced here on a hardlinked copy with root's before bytes (check-analysis-seal-adapter exit 1 at analysis-seal-owner-only-semantically-false). With root's after bytes: exit 0, 16/16.",
   "ownProcessFinding": "My v1/v2 affected-caller search covered foundation/workflows/native close_run callers and omitted security/, so the analysis-seal adapter was not in my v2 regression set. My v2 sentence that close_run refusal 'class names are unchanged' was wrong for the semantic replay disagreement case (see qualification)."
  },
  {
   "id": "SI-2",
   "severity": "assessed: no misrouting after correction; before-bytes also had a latent opposite misroute",
   "title": "Lawful typed refusals vs host faults at the SEAL adapter, over actual close_run paths",
   "evidence": "Real-path probe (integrated copy): lawful Run ADMIT; reminted semantically false Run REJECT SEAL_CLOSE_RUN_REFUSED:EVALUATOR_COMPLETE_PROOF_REPLAY with cause exactly IM.CompleteReplayMismatch; structural REFERENCE_IDENTITY and corrupt blob BLOB_DIGEST REJECT with cause IM.C.AdmissionError; missing proof object REJECT with cause IM.EvidenceUnavailable; a declared atom owner refusal raised inside the replay stack is normalized by close_run and REJECTs (cause IM.C.AdmissionError, inner AtomAdmissionError); an undeclared same-named 'AdmissionError' class, a RuntimeError carrying an owner key, and a TypeError inside the comparison all PROPAGATE unchanged; lawful Run ADMITs again after restore. Same probe on before bytes: the semantic false Run PROPAGATES (root failure) and the undeclared same-named 'AdmissionError' class inside the stack is misrouted to REJECT (name matching). The correction fixes both directions.",
   "typeIdentity": "IM is the security loader's own identity copy (security_identity_model_v3); close_run normalizes its separate replay stack (composition_identity3) declared outcomes into IM classes, so except IM.C.AdmissionError is the exact-identity boundary for every declared owner refusal including CompleteReplayMismatch and EvidenceUnavailable."
  },
  {
   "id": "SI-3",
   "severity": "assessed: boundary respected; advisory SI-A1",
   "title": "SEAL boundary does not impose the retained-regeneration public route at a live host",
   "evidence": "admit_analysis_seal raises only the security-local Reject key SEAL_CLOSE_RUN_REFUSED:<first diagnostic line>; Reject carries no termination (hasPublicTermination false in every probe row) and SEAL_CLOSE_RUN_REFUSED has no D9/public-detail mapping in the security model. The chained cause is the origin-free identity condition CompleteReplayMismatch, not the RegenerationMismatch retained carrier, so the outer host keeps the origin decision (live first-party contradiction -> complete-replay-mismatch:host-internal). identity EvidenceStore.prepare and run_termination_model.retained_population likewise propagate the condition uncarried; only the retained restore boundary maps it to RegenerationMismatch.",
   "advisory": "SI-A1: an outer host projection must select by the Reject __cause__ type (as the maintained typed controls assert), never by parsing the diagnostic text the Reject key embeds. No outer live-host fault projection exists in the reviewed files."
  },
  {
