   "severity": "assessed: remedy retains both protections",
   "title": "QF-I1 control correction keeps schema-first order and a distinct owner-parity refusal",
   "evidence": "Corrected checker on the integrated copy: exit 0, 41 rows. Discrimination probe with the unmodified production model: illegal pair (provider-protocol, HOST.IO_FAILURE) is refused by schema alone (ValidationError anyOf at /termination) and by validate_envelope with the same schema error; the structurally legal wrong pair (host-io, HOST.IO_FAILURE) is ADMITTED by schema alone and refused only by EVALUATOR_FAULT_ENVELOPE_PARITY (termination differs from routed); exit and public-detail mismatches remain parity refusals; the lawful envelope admits; validate_envelope still validates profile before parity. evaluator_fault_model.v3.py, evaluator-fault-observation.schema.v3.json, evaluator3 common and command-envelope schemas and workflow_projection_model.v3.py are byte-identical to the verified source37 overlay, so no production law or order changed. My earlier alternatives (accept earlier refusal / parity before validation) are not needed; root's separate controls are the better shape.",
